In this problem, you're basically just solving for 2F(n+1)-1 where F(n+1) is the n+1 Fibonacci number. So 2 * (the n+1 Fibonacci number) - 1. Recursion and other solutions will take a long time, so instead the solution that usually works is just a for loop that solves this equation, which is O(n).

Here is his code in JS:
const n = parseInt(readline());
let a = 1;
let b = 1;

for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    [a, b] = [b, a + b + 1]
}

console.log(a);
